  "result": "Okay \u2014 just answering, then.\n\nIf I could change one thing, I wouldn't end war or poverty directly. I'd give everyone a pause they're forced to feel: the moment before you speak or act on anger, you'd hear what you're about to do exactly the way the other person will hear it. Not as guilt. Just as information you can't un-know.\n\nI think so much cruelty, online and off, survives because it's abstract. We get to stay inside our own intention \u2014 *I was joking, I was scared, I was right* \u2014 and never have to live for a second inside the impact. If that gap closed, even a little, people would still disagree, still be selfish, still make mistakes. But they'd have to do it knowingly.\n\nAnd I suspect most people, actually knowing, would choose something softer.",
